Findings below. Everything is vanilla JS + Alpine.js served from `public/` (Firebase Hosting); the "native" app is a Preact shell in `public/mobile/` that opens this same page in a WebView.

---

## 1. Which files render the OOS page

**The Order of Service page is `service-builder.html` / `service-builder.js`.** (Confusingly named — CONTEXT.md calls it the "Order of Service editor" and explicitly deprecates the name "builder".)

- `C:\Users\jono1\Professional Projects\Mosaic-Project\main-worktrees\MS-303\public\service-builder.html` (1342 lines) — markup, Alpine `x-data="serviceForm()"`.
- `C:\Users\jono1\Professional Projects\Mosaic-Project\main-worktrees\MS-303\public\service-builder.js` (2537 lines) — the `serviceForm()` component, starting at line 331.
- Definition of record: `CONTEXT.md:374-376` — *"**Order of Service editor**: The structured liturgy surface (`service-builder.html`) launched from the Service Calendar… _Avoid_: OOS Editor (ambiguous), Order of Service Builder, builder"*.

**There is no native Preact OOS screen.** The mobile app routes to the same desktop page in-shell:
- `public\mobile\app.js:250-259`
  ```js
  if (route === "serviceBuilder") {
    if (data.forget) data.forget("services");
    var d = (params && params.date) || "";
    if (!d) { M.navParams = {}; location.hash = "#/calendar"; return; }
