## 4. Existing next/previous navigation to copy

Three good precedents:

**(a) Windowed prev/next over a list of dates — closest match.** `public\recurring-events.js:449-476`
```js
get hasEarlier() { return Grid.previousAnchor(this.allDates, this.anchor, this.windowSize) !== null; }
get hasLater()   { return Grid.nextAnchor(this.allDates, this.anchor, this.windowSize) !== null; }
async earlier() { const at = Grid.previousAnchor(...); if (at === null) return; this.anchor = at; await this.loadWindow(); }
async later()   { ... }
async backToToday() { this.anchor = Dates.todayStr(); await this.loadWindow(); }
```
Core helpers: `public\recurring-roster-core.js:350-360` (`previousAnchor`, `nextAnchor`).
Markup with chevrons + disabled states: `public\recurring-events.html:472-487`
```html
<button @click="earlier()" :disabled="!hasEarlier || gridLoading" class="m-btn m-btn--quiet m-btn--sm re-motion re-press re-focus">
  <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-[18px]">chevron_left</span>
  <span class="m-btn__label">Earlier</span>
</button>
<span class="re-paging__win" x-text="windowLabel"></span>
<button @click="later()" :disabled="!hasLater || gridLoading" ...>
```

**(b) Month stepper with `< >` + "Today".** `public\calendar.js:1137-1138`
```js
prevMonth() { return this.goToMonth(shiftMonth(this.month, -1)); },
nextMonth() { return this.goToMonth(shiftMonth(this.month, 1)); },
```
Markup (desktop `cal-stepper` and phone variant, both with `aria-label`): `public\calendar.html:341-349` and `:413-421`.

**(c) Month paging on the Away page.** `public\away.js:421-427` (`prevMonths()` / `nextMonths()`), plus swipe at `:508` — `if (dx < 0) this.nextMonths(); else this.prevMonths();` (mirrored at `public\calendar.js:591`). Swipe is an existing gesture idiom if you want it on mobile.

**Nothing navigates record-to-record today** (no next-hymn, next-person, next-service arrows anywhere). The OOS page's only header nav is a back link: `public\service-builder.html:213-216`.

Design-system button classes available: `m-btn m-btn--quiet m-btn--sm`, `m-icon-btn m-icon-btn--sm m-icon-btn--ghost`, `material-symbols-outlined` glyphs `chevron_left` / `chevron_right`.

