i.e. start = earliest of (today, earliest *stored* service date) rather than a fixed 2023-07-09; end = the later of (120 days out, latest stored service date) rather than two years. Both lists then filter to `>= today` unless "history" is toggled (`screens-content.js:406`; `service-calendar.js:525` `const showHistory = false`). So desktop and mobile disagree on both ends of the range, and neither derives its bounds from a shared module.
